INSTRUCTIONS
1. You shall specifically admit or deny each Request, or set forth in detail the reasons why You cannot truthfully admit or deny the Requests.
2. If You deny, either in whole or in part, any Request for Admission served on You, state the factual and legal basis for each denial or partial denial, including identifying any Documents and Communications that are part of that basis.
3. When good faith requires You to qualify an answer or deny only a part thereof, You shall specify what is true and qualify or deny the remainder.
4. Lack of information or knowledge may not be given as a reason for failure to admit or deny a Request unless You state You have made reasonable inquiry and the information known or readily obtained or obtainable by You is insufficient to enable You to admit or deny.
5. You may not object to a Request solely because You consider a Request to present a genuine issue for trial.
